# UST.G3BD Sparse Deligne Quotient Decision Theorem

## Purpose

G3BC replaces the selected pairing-one dual only modulo the integral period
lattice. That is enough to decide the physical Deligne class directly, but it
does not by itself license a coordinate-level G3AU normal-row substitution.
G3BD makes the direct quotient route exact and executable.

Write the normalized eta9 readout as

```text
beta_C = [R_B] in C^248 / Pi_C(V_Z).
```

## Exact zero certificate

Let `p_1,...,p_m` be hash-bound columns of `Pi_C` coming from integrally
normalized Betti cycles. If integers `n_1,...,n_m` satisfy

```text
R_B = sum_j n_j p_j
```

in all 248 exact coordinates, then `beta_C=0`. This implication does not need
the supplied columns to span the full period lattice: one genuine lattice
membership witness is sufficient.

## Exact nonzero certificate

Let `ell` be an exact complex-linear covector. Suppose a separate scope
certificate proves that `ell` annihilates the full integral period lattice, or
the corresponding certified saturated detecting quotient, and interval
arithmetic proves

```text
0 not in ell(R_B).
```

Then `beta_C` is nonzero. Annihilating only an incomplete list of period
columns is not enough for this branch.

The more general and usually more useful certificate is a dual-lattice
character. Let `chi:C^248 -> R` be exact real-linear and suppose

```text
chi(Pi_C(V_Z)) is contained in Z.
```

If an interval enclosure of `chi(R_B)` contains no integer, then `R_B` cannot
be a period and `beta_C` is nonzero. The annihilator theorem is the special
case in which `chi` is zero on every period. Unlike that special case, a
dual-lattice character can exist when the period lattice spans all of
`C^248`.

## Consequence

The two branches give an exact direct exit for the physical flat
Deligne/Brauer value:

```text
integer period membership  -> beta_C = 0,
dual-lattice separation    -> beta_C != 0.
```

None of these branches requires G3AU. That normal operator remains a useful early
prefilter only after period descent or a same-lift G3AR binding has been
proved. Thus G3BD avoids both an unnecessary `248 x 1509` period matrix and an
invalid representative substitution.

## Execution

```powershell
python build_ust_g3bd_sparse_deligne_quotient_decision.py
python verify_ust_g3bd_sparse_deligne_quotient_decision.py
```

The builder executes one exact zero fixture, one annihilator fixture and one
nonintegral dual-character fixture in 248 coordinates. All are explicitly
nonphysical.

